hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"18525","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Sufyan informed us, from Jabir, from al-Sha'bi, from Abdullah ibn Thabit, he said: Umar ibn al-Khattab came to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and said: O Messenger of Allah, I passed by a brother of mine of Banu Qurayzah, and he wrote for me comprehensive passages from the Torah, shall I not present them to you. He said: The face of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, changed. Abdullah, meaning Ibn Thabit, said: I said to him: Do you not see what is on the face of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. Umar said: We are pleased with Allah Almighty as Lord, and with Islam as religion, and with Muhammad, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, as Messenger. He said: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was relieved, and said: By the One in Whose Hand is the soul of Muhammad, if Musa were alive among you, then you followed him and left me, you would have gone astray. You are my portion of the nations, and I am your portion of the prophets."
